No git history. Let me look at the full `merge_with_prev` and understand the use-after-free. The crash is a WRITE 8 in `merge_with_prev`. Let me look at the lines that write.

In `merge_with_prev`:
```c
first->next = second->next;
first->next->prev = first;   // WRITE
RL_LEN (first) += RL_LEN (second);
if (second->next_isolate)
    second->next_isolate->prev_isolate = second->prev_isolate;
else if (second->next->prev_isolate == second)
    second->next->prev_isolate = second->prev_isolate;
if (second->prev_isolate)
    second->prev_isolate->next_isolate = second->next_isolate;
first->next_isolate = second->next_isolate;
fribidi_free (second);
```

The use-after-free WRITE 8. Let me think about the scenario. `merge_with_prev` frees `second`. Then the caller continues iterating. In `compact_list`:
```c
for_run_list (list, list)
    if (RL_TYPE (list->prev) == RL_TYPE (list) ...)
        list = merge_with_prev (list);
```

After `merge_with_prev(list)`, `list` is set to `first` (the prev). Then the loop continues with `list = list->next`. But wait, `merge_with_prev` frees `second` which was `list`. Then returns `first`. The loop macro `for_run_list` advances `list = list->next`. 

Let me look at the `for_run_list` macro.

